WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.609 --> 00:00:06.040
I was bored in school.

00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:07.760
Lots of us were and

00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:09.600
when kids are bored and restless,

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:12.020
schools usually blame the kid.

00:00:12.020 --> 00:00:16.520
1 in 5 high school boys diagnosed with ADHD

00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:19.470
Millions are given drugs to try to make them sit still

00:00:19.470 --> 00:00:21.680
I was the rowdy kid, that was the bad kid.

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:23.360
So they really pressured my parents

00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:25.620
to actually put me on ADHD medication

00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:26.400
Adderall.

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:28.020
Yeah, Adderall, Ritalin...

00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:29.880
it was like I had been lobotomized.

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:32.040
My parents said, "This is not our son."

00:00:32.060 --> 00:00:34.059
They then sent him to other schools.

00:00:34.059 --> 00:00:35.310
he hated them all.

00:00:35.310 --> 00:00:37.700
I would come home and I would sometimes just cry.

00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:38.820
What better things could I have been doing

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:40.800
during that time where I was just sitting

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:43.300
in a classroom having information chucked at me.

00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:44.840
So what did you do?

00:00:44.840 --> 00:00:45.840
I left.

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:47.220
He left because he heard about a school

00:00:47.220 --> 00:00:49.020
that teaches in a different way.

00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:52.240
Like ok how do we actually increase our knowledge?

00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:57.140
The school is the Academy of Thought and Industry

00:00:57.140 --> 00:00:59.240
but the school costs money.

00:00:59.240 --> 00:01:03.400
I got a job at a coffee shop.

00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:05.840
to work here he got up at 3 in the morning

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:10.430
by 3:30 he was in the shop setting up tables and chairs

00:01:10.430 --> 00:01:12.520
cleaning the counters

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:16.600
I would get the bacon frying

00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:18.740
get all the breakfast items ready.

00:01:18.750 --> 00:01:21.040
Hard work just to go to this school.

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:24.280
Academy of Thought and Industry, it sounds Soviet.

00:01:24.280 --> 00:01:26.380
I want my students to think with their minds

00:01:26.380 --> 00:01:28.700
and understand the world and I want them to

00:01:28.700 --> 00:01:30.200
get stuff done.

00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:32.100
Michael Strong started the academy

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:33.240
by telling parents

00:01:33.240 --> 00:01:36.200
“Kids learn better by doing actual work.”

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:38.120
Teens need responsibility.

00:01:38.120 --> 00:01:41.280
Ben Franklin, Andrew Carnegie, Thomas Edison,

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:42.240
started their careers

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:43.820
at the age of 12 or 13.

00:01:43.820 --> 00:01:46.660
Yeah, that was abusive child labor.

00:01:46.660 --> 00:01:47.920
I worked as a teen.

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:49.120
I loved it.

00:01:49.120 --> 00:01:52.660
At his schools, there are now two with more on the way,

00:01:52.660 --> 00:01:54.460
Students get Fridays off

00:01:54.460 --> 00:01:56.600
to work on their own projects.

00:01:56.600 --> 00:01:58.040
there are no lectures

00:01:58.040 --> 00:02:01.280
instead students read and discuss things.

00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:02.840
Because they're still people

00:02:02.840 --> 00:02:05.380
and people still have certain drives

00:02:05.380 --> 00:02:08.080
That’s very different from schools Strong attended.

00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:09.240
and hated.

00:02:09.240 --> 00:02:11.720
School is 13 years of how to be passive

00:02:11.720 --> 00:02:14.020
and how to be dependent.

00:02:14.020 --> 00:02:16.620
The Republican controlled House of Representatives…

00:02:16.620 --> 00:02:20.660
Sit still, read, listen to your elders, repeat.

00:02:20.660 --> 00:02:22.160
Anyone know the effects?

00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:25.060
School is about aim, aim, aim, aim, aim,

00:02:25.060 --> 00:02:26.380
and never get stuff done.

00:02:26.380 --> 00:02:28.400
So I want students who let's just go out there

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:30.720
get stuff done, fail, get up, try again...

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:33.020
That's how we become creators, entrepreneurs...

00:02:33.020 --> 00:02:35.680
We want them to do what they love now.

00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:39.880
Cade was given projects like: start a business today

00:02:39.880 --> 00:02:42.840
Why was that more interesting than studying history?

00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:44.280
Or going to science projects?

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:45.980
Because the money, because the money.

00:02:45.980 --> 00:02:47.840
I'm currently working on making

00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:50.100
a web-based chat application.

00:02:50.110 --> 00:02:52.600
Students study what they care about.

00:02:52.600 --> 00:02:54.150
I wanna be a programmer.

00:02:54.150 --> 00:02:55.150
I love programming.

00:02:55.150 --> 00:02:56.830
We got to create a project

00:02:56.830 --> 00:03:00.470
and immediately start feeling the rewards of it.

00:03:00.470 --> 00:03:03.540
I was doing a few sketches for the costume designs.

00:03:03.540 --> 00:03:06.400
I actually work at a paintball place.

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:07.900
If they love paintball,

00:03:07.900 --> 00:03:10.240
then they should do a business in that.

00:03:12.080 --> 00:03:14.500
Dorian Domi started a music business.

00:03:14.500 --> 00:03:16.260
At this point in my career,

00:03:16.260 --> 00:03:18.460
I’ve booked almost 200 bands.

00:03:18.460 --> 00:03:21.980
His music festival, brings in tens of thousands of dollars.

00:03:21.980 --> 00:03:23.780
We have students who have done websites

00:03:23.780 --> 00:03:26.220
for American Idol finalists.

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:29.300
These people use the website then as their own?

00:03:29.300 --> 00:03:31.420
For about 9 months and then he fired the team,

00:03:31.420 --> 00:03:33.240
a high school team, and got a better team.

00:03:33.240 --> 00:03:35.200
That was a great experience for my students,

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:36.840
to get fired by a client

00:03:36.840 --> 00:03:38.700
is actually a really good experience.

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:39.860
You do that several times and

00:03:39.860 --> 00:03:41.760
that's how you get better at getting stuff done.

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:44.520
So companies hire Strong’s students.

00:03:44.520 --> 00:03:47.470
Cade got a marketing job right out of high school.

00:03:47.470 --> 00:03:48.620
At a place called Launchpeer

00:03:48.620 --> 00:03:49.860
which I currently am at today.

00:03:49.860 --> 00:03:51.500
People say, "You gotta go to college."

00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:54.400
Well, look at me.

00:03:54.409 --> 00:03:57.000
Most of Strong’s students do go to college.

00:03:57.000 --> 00:03:58.460
We've had students be admitted to

00:03:58.460 --> 00:04:00.060
top liberal arts colleges.

00:04:00.069 --> 00:04:01.480
Bard, Bennington

00:04:01.490 --> 00:04:02.580
‘course they do well.

00:04:02.580 --> 00:04:05.299
You're charging fat tuition.

00:04:05.299 --> 00:04:07.320
Only rich kids can afford to go there

00:04:07.320 --> 00:04:08.890
and they're going to do well.

00:04:08.890 --> 00:04:13.330
The kind of kids that we get come from all walks of life.

00:04:13.330 --> 00:04:15.610
We had a student from New Jersey

00:04:15.610 --> 00:04:17.680
he was incapable of functioning

00:04:17.680 --> 00:04:20.260
in the highly structured public school system.

00:04:20.260 --> 00:04:22.960
In middle school, elementary school,

00:04:22.960 --> 00:04:25.520
I was, you know, incredibly socially isolated.

00:04:25.520 --> 00:04:29.400
In the public schools he needed a full time aide.

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:31.540
He was costing the state an enormous amount of money.

00:04:31.540 --> 00:04:34.380
He came to our school, he did not need an aide.

00:04:34.380 --> 00:04:36.540
Coming here is just healing.

00:04:36.540 --> 00:04:37.740
It's incredible.

00:04:39.580 --> 00:04:41.260
So much so that some students

00:04:41.260 --> 00:04:43.080
wake up at 3 in the morning

00:04:43.080 --> 00:04:45.560
to go to work to help pay tuition.

00:04:45.580 --> 00:04:49.500
It was me choosing my life

